{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-switch-panel-shop-01","date":"2026-11-26","lens":"gap-6","surface":"panel","area":"panel/shop","refs":["F-panel-808"],"severity":"S3","title":"A price or discount typed with a decimal point becomes a figure 100 or 10 times bigger in a member message","what":"In Messages & offers, the amount, discount and number boxes of a ready message throw away every character that is not a plain digit, including the decimal point and digits typed on a Hindi keyboard. Typing or pasting '1,499.00' leaves 149900, so the message says the price is about 1.5 lakh rupees; a '12.5' per cent discount becomes 125 per cent. Hindi-keyboard digits vanish, so the box stays empty and the send button stays off with no reason given.","expected":"The box either keeps the amount the owner meant (1,499) or says plainly that only whole rupees can be typed. It never quietly turns one number into another before it goes to every app member.","evidence":["apps/dashboard/src/crm/shop/MessagesSection.tsx:802-807","apps/dashboard/src/crm/shop/MessagesSection.tsx:819-821"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"message-amount-box-drops-decimal-point","who":"owners and front desk sending offers, and the members who read them","how_often":"whenever an amount or discount is typed or pasted with a decimal point","fix_line":"Read amounts with the same rupee reader the product price box already uses, and refuse what it cannot read with a clear line","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
